884 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The epidemiology of dengue infection is changing in Sri Lanka. An essentially childhood predominant disease in the 1990s, dengue has now become an infection of adults with a reciprocal reduction in incidence among children. )
/E (The epidemiology of dengue infection is changing in Sri Lanka. An essentially childhood predominant disease in the 1990s, dengue has now become an infection of adults with a reciprocal reduction in incidence among children. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4 5]
>>
endobj
885 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Our case fatality rate which was 9.8% in 1989, has come down to 0.05% this year. The credit should go to the clinicians, the medical officers and the nursing officers who work tirelessly, look after the patients and follow the current guidelines. The last guideline was published in November 2012 by the Epidemiology Unit of the Ministry of Health Sri Lanka. This was contributed to by many and the enforcement of the guidelines through death reviews was instrumental in bringing down the mortality. )
/E (Our case fatality rate which was 9.8% in 1989, has come down to 0.05% this year. The credit should go to the clinicians, the medical officers and the nursing officers who work tirelessly, look after the patients and follow the current guidelines. The last guideline was published in November 2012 by the Epidemiology Unit of the Ministry of Health Sri Lanka. This was contributed to by many and the enforcement of the guidelines through death reviews was instrumental in bringing down the mortality. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
886 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (In addition, we have the National Dengue Control Unit and the Epidemiology Unit and their health care personnel in the community who work to the best of their capacity to curb the case load. If we are to bring the mortality rate to a level closer to zero, we need to go beyond the currently available guidelines. We consider that the time is opportune, as we have clinicians who have amassed years of experience in managing difficult cases of dengue. )
/E (In addition, we have the National Dengue Control Unit and the Epidemiology Unit and their health care personnel in the community who work to the best of their capacity to curb the case load. If we are to bring the mortality rate to a level closer to zero, we need to go beyond the currently available guidelines. We consider that the time is opportune, as we have clinicians who have amassed years of experience in managing difficult cases of dengue. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
