/T (Dengue is a mosquito-borne infection caused by a single-stranded RNA virus belonging to the family Flaviviridae, genus Flavivirus. Four antigenically distinct serotypes of DENV, DENV-1, DENV-2, DENV-3, and DENV-4 are known to cause infections. There is considerable genetic variation within each serotype, with distinct subtypes.)
/E (Dengue is a mosquito-borne infection caused by a single-stranded RNA virus belonging to the family Flaviviridae, genus Flavivirus. Four antigenically distinct serotypes of DENV, DENV-1, DENV-2, DENV-3, and DENV-4 are known to cause infections. There is considerable genetic variation within each serotype, with distinct subtypes.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3 4]
