1121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Bleeding is a common complication in dengue illness and is multifactorial. It can occur in both DF and DHF patients. In paediatric age groups, bleeding usually occurs after prolonged shock. However, in adults, bleeding can occur without shock. In some patients, bleeding can be overt in the form of haematemesis, melaena, and menorrhagia. However, in most patients bleeding is occult. )
/E (Bleeding is a common complication in dengue illness and is multifactorial. It can occur in both DF and DHF patients. In paediatric age groups, bleeding usually occurs after prolonged shock. However, in adults, bleeding can occur without shock. In some patients, bleeding can be overt in the form of haematemesis, melaena, and menorrhagia. However, in most patients bleeding is occult. )
/Pg 30 0 R
/K [9 10]
>>
endobj
