1147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Circulatory shock is a life-threatening condition of circulatory failure, causing inadequate oxygen delivery to meet cellular metabolic needs and oxygen consumption requirements, producing cellular and tissue hypoxia. In DSS inadequate tissue perfusion is mainly due to reduction in the intravascular volume due to plasma leak or haemorrhage. )
/E (Circulatory shock is a life-threatening condition of circulatory failure, causing inadequate oxygen delivery to meet cellular metabolic needs and oxygen consumption requirements, producing cellular and tissue hypoxia. In DSS inadequate tissue perfusion is mainly due to reduction in the intravascular volume due to plasma leak or haemorrhage. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [7 8]
>>
