/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (If the plasma leakage is insignificant, the patient will compensate, and changes in the vital parameters or urine output may not be obvious. However, if the leaking is significant, the patient may not be able to compensate. Significant plasma leakage or plasma leakage with bleeding are the main causes of shock in dengue. Persistent shock will result in further bleeding, organ failure and death. )
/E (If the plasma leakage is insignificant, the patient will compensate, and changes in the vital parameters or urine output may not be obvious. However, if the leaking is significant, the patient may not be able to compensate. Significant plasma leakage or plasma leakage with bleeding are the main causes of shock in dengue. Persistent shock will result in further bleeding, organ failure and death. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [7]
>>
