/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Fluid replacement is the most important measure in the management of DF/DHF. Adequate fluid replacement is essential to avoid dehydration during the febrile phase, and to avoid shock due to significant volume loss in the critical phase. Careful fluid replacement during the latter part of the critical phase, equilibrium phase and recovery phase in a DHF patient is important to avoid fluid overload.)
/E (Fluid replacement is the most important measure in the management of DF/DHF. Adequate fluid replacement is essential to avoid dehydration during the febrile phase, and to avoid shock due to significant volume loss in the critical phase. Careful fluid replacement during the latter part of the critical phase, equilibrium phase and recovery phase in a DHF patient is important to avoid fluid overload.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [1]
>>
