/S /H2
/T (There may be a haemodynamically unstable patient who is dehydrated \(due to persistent vomiting, diarrhoea or reduced oral intake\) in addition to plasma leakage at the time of admission. In the resuscitation of such a patient, the degree of dehydration should be considered, and more crystalloids should be given initially to replace the deficit.)
/E (There may be a haemodynamically unstable patient who is dehydrated \(due to persistent vomiting, diarrhoea or reduced oral intake\) in addition to plasma leakage at the time of admission. In the resuscitation of such a patient, the degree of dehydration should be considered, and more crystalloids should be given initially to replace the deficit.)
