/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Bleeding in dengue is commonly occult \(can occur in muscles, peritoneal cavity or pleural cavity\). However, petechial haemorrhages and microscopic haematuria are seen commonly. Menstrual bleeding can be excessive and intermenstrual bleeding is not uncommon. Haematamesis, melaena, and gross haematuria are uncommon overt bleeds. Therefore, when seeing a patient;)
/E (Bleeding in dengue is commonly occult \(can occur in muscles, peritoneal cavity or pleural cavity\). However, petechial haemorrhages and microscopic haematuria are seen commonly. Menstrual bleeding can be excessive and intermenstrual bleeding is not uncommon. Haematamesis, melaena, and gross haematuria are uncommon overt bleeds. Therefore, when seeing a patient;)
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
