/T (Ask about the presence of bleeding per vagina. This could be menstrual bleeding, intermenstrual bleeding or even post-menopausal bleeding. Young girls who have not attained menarche may develop their first bleeding while having dengue. If bleeding is not present on admission, advise the patient to inform the health staff if bleeding develops. Even normal menstrual bleeding may contribute to shock in a DHF patient. )
/E (Ask about the presence of bleeding per vagina. This could be menstrual bleeding, intermenstrual bleeding or even post-menopausal bleeding. Young girls who have not attained menarche may develop their first bleeding while having dengue. If bleeding is not present on admission, advise the patient to inform the health staff if bleeding develops. Even normal menstrual bleeding may contribute to shock in a DHF patient. )
/Pg 59 0 R
/K [6]
>>
