/S /H2
/T (9.3 PROTHROMBIN COMPLEX CONCENTRATE \(PCC\))
/E (9.3 PROTHROMBIN COMPLEX CONCENTRATE \(PCC\))
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1844 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (PCC can be used to replace factors II, VII, IX and X. It has the added advantage that it will not contribute to fluid overload, unlike FFP. PCC should only be used in patients with liver failure and active bleeding.)
/E (PCC can be used to replace factors II, VII, IX and X. It has the added advantage that it will not contribute to fluid overload, unlike FFP. PCC should only be used in patients with liver failure and active bleeding.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1845 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (9.4 RECOMBINANT FACTOR VII )
/E (9.4 RECOMBINANT FACTOR VII )
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1846 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (There is no evidence to support the use of recombinant factor VII in DHF patients with bleeding due to prolonged shock, DIC or multi-organ failure. Therefore, the use of factor VII as a treatment for bleeding in DHF is not recommended. Recombinant factor VII is useful only in patients who have massive bleeding due to a specific cause such as bleeding peptic ulcer or bleeding from a specific place \(e.g., bleeding from the nose\) before surgical intervention. This helps to buy time for specific surgical treatments like banding, cauterisation etc. It should be used only if definite plans are there for surgical intervention as the arrest of bleeding with recombinant factor VII is only temporary due to its short half-life.)
/E (There is no evidence to support the use of recombinant factor VII in DHF patients with bleeding due to prolonged shock, DIC or multi-organ failure. Therefore, the use of factor VII as a treatment for bleeding in DHF is not recommended. Recombinant factor VII is useful only in patients who have massive bleeding due to a specific cause such as bleeding peptic ulcer or bleeding from a specific place \(e.g., bleeding from the nose\) before surgical intervention. This helps to buy time for specific surgical treatments like banding, cauterisation etc. It should be used only if definite plans are there for surgical intervention as the arrest of bleeding with recombinant factor VII is only temporary due to its short half-life.)
/Pg 64 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
