/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Liver involvement is common and usually self-limiting in dengue. However, it is also the most significant organ involvement which can lead to a fatal outcome in dengue. Significant liver injury is usually due to prolonged shock or repeated episodes of shock. However, it could occur in the absence of shock at times due to persistent intravascular hypovolaemia \(without causing shock\) for several hours or rarely due to severe dengue hepatitis.)
/E (Liver involvement is common and usually self-limiting in dengue. However, it is also the most significant organ involvement which can lead to a fatal outcome in dengue. Significant liver injury is usually due to prolonged shock or repeated episodes of shock. However, it could occur in the absence of shock at times due to persistent intravascular hypovolaemia \(without causing shock\) for several hours or rarely due to severe dengue hepatitis.)
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [1]
>>
