/T (With ongoing leaking of plasma in DHF, it is important to identify the intravascular volume status and fluid responsiveness. By this time most of the patients would have received a significant volume of crystalloids and/or dextran. If the HCT is high and the recommended dextran volume is not completed, dextran should be given. If the recommended dextran volume is exceeded, 4-5% albumin could be used as the resuscitative fluid especially when serum albumin <3 g/L.)
/E (With ongoing leaking of plasma in DHF, it is important to identify the intravascular volume status and fluid responsiveness. By this time most of the patients would have received a significant volume of crystalloids and/or dextran. If the HCT is high and the recommended dextran volume is not completed, dextran should be given. If the recommended dextran volume is exceeded, 4-5% albumin could be used as the resuscitative fluid especially when serum albumin <3 g/L.)
