/P 4014 0 R
/T (For patients with AKI, in the absence of facilities for HD/ CRRT or if the patient is having persistently low BP, acute peritoneal dialysis \(PD\) preferably using a flexible coil peritoneal dialysis catheter \(which enables smooth functioning of the PD catheter\) should be considered. If the patient is in lactataemia, a bicarbonate-based PD fluid should be used instead of the lactate buffer. PD will have the additional benefit of removal of fluid accumulated in the peritoneal cavity during the leaking phase which will improve renal haemodynamics in return. It also has the added benefit of not requiring anticoagulants unlike in CRRT or SLED.)
/E (For patients with AKI, in the absence of facilities for HD/ CRRT or if the patient is having persistently low BP, acute peritoneal dialysis \(PD\) preferably using a flexible coil peritoneal dialysis catheter \(which enables smooth functioning of the PD catheter\) should be considered. If the patient is in lactataemia, a bicarbonate-based PD fluid should be used instead of the lactate buffer. PD will have the additional benefit of removal of fluid accumulated in the peritoneal cavity during the leaking phase which will improve renal haemodynamics in return. It also has the added benefit of not requiring anticoagulants unlike in CRRT or SLED.)
/Pg 71 0 R
>>
