/T (Therefore, empirical treatment with calcium is justifiable in patients with large pleural effusion/ascites. Myocardial involvement is an uncommon finding in dengue \(unless following DSS\) and is very unlikely to cause death in a patient with DHF. However, such patients could easily develop pulmonary oedema due to fluid overload.)
/E (Therefore, empirical treatment with calcium is justifiable in patients with large pleural effusion/ascites. Myocardial involvement is an uncommon finding in dengue \(unless following DSS\) and is very unlikely to cause death in a patient with DHF. However, such patients could easily develop pulmonary oedema due to fluid overload.)
