/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Spun HCT refers to the direct measurement of haematocrit using centrifugation. Blood is collected in a capillary tube and spun in a centrifuge, separating the blood into its components: red blood cells \(RBCs\), plasma, and the buffy coat \(white blood cells and platelets\). )
/E (Spun HCT refers to the direct measurement of haematocrit using centrifugation. Blood is collected in a capillary tube and spun in a centrifuge, separating the blood into its components: red blood cells \(RBCs\), plasma, and the buffy coat \(white blood cells and platelets\). )
/Pg 88 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
